Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Graph  PD  Notation  and Caps", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.924093587385165*^9, 3.924093606767956*^9}, {
  3.932822963923808*^9, 3.9328229683911333`*^9}, {3.932829611010184*^9, 
  3.932829611779834*^9}, {3.933670465234143*^9, 
  3.933670465725749*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"12a44dc9-ec43-47b9-aa69-\
6aa8957fc528"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We begin with a discussion of graph PD notation that will be used \
throughout this and the other notebooks. \n\nLet \[CapitalGamma] be a ribbon \
graph for a plane trivalent graph G.  The ribbon structure of \[CapitalGamma] \
is encoded by the cyclic ordering of the edges at each vertex, and the \
ribbons are assumed to lay flat on the plane.  To encode the the graph we may \
first blowup to create a 3-cycle at each vertex.  We then number the edges of \
each 3 cycle consecutively as shown in the figure below.  The starting point \
on each 3-cycle is arbitrary but in each case we go counterclockwise around \
the cycle.  See below.\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
