 "\nFor the K_4 above, we obtain the following Graph PD Notation:\nK4 = \
M[7,9,2,1] M[9,8,4,6]M[6,5,3,2]M[12,11,5,4]M[11,10,1,3]M[8,7,10,12]\n\nA \
state graph for \[CapitalGamma] may be obtained by choosing a clasp or a \
buckle (see below) at each edge of the original graph.  Collectively, these \
will be referred to as interactions. Note that the clasp is topologically the \
same as an untwisted ribbon.  The twist and the diamond are used to indicate \
that any harmonic coloring of the state graph must color the two boundary \
components of the ribbon with different colors.  \n",
