Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Generating Pre-Caps ", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.924093617005208*^9, 3.924093626077908*^9}, {
   3.933429580459854*^9, 3.9334295862459497`*^9}, 3.9334305383732347`*^9, {
   3.933431972119795*^9, 
   3.93343197398663*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a098b492-bde1-47cc-8da5-\
959924f3bc8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Our initial step is to generate a list of all permutations.  Each \
permutation generated below is given as a 6-component vector \[Sigma] = \
{a,b,c,d,e,f} whose components consist of the numbers 1 through 6.  This can \
be converted to a list of ordered pairs consisting of the component and its \
position. The permutation \[Sigma] = {a,b,c,d,e,f} would correspond to the \
list {{1,a},{2,b},{3,c},{4,d},{5,e},{6,f}}.  This can be thought of as a list \
of arcs as shown.  For example, \[Sigma] = {6,4,5,3,2,1} corresponds to the \
ordered pairs {{1,6},{2,4},{3,5},{4,3},{5,2},{6,1}}.  Each ordered pair {a,b} \
can be converted directly to an arc, denoted arc[a,b].  Pictorially, we \
obtain the following:\n",
