Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["From  PreCaps  to  Caps", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.924093617005208*^9, 
  3.924093626077908*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d9ad33b7-2dd2-4b50-967c-\
6cd035a5c827"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each PreCap computed above provides a list of arcs joining spokes (numbered \
1 to 6), but we wish to convert this to a list of arcs which are compatible \
with smoothings at the spokes.   For example, the fourth PreCap above is \
given by:\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"arc", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "6"}], "]"}], "2"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"arc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "]"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"arc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "]"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"arc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "]"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"arc", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}], "]"}]}]],
  CellChangeTimes->{
   3.9241081362494097`*^9, 3.924181660970681*^9, 3.924595384086519*^9, 
    3.9259875010567493`*^9, 3.926163862190439*^9, 3.926163907367725*^9, 
    3.926508060426139*^9, 3.927107040652108*^9, 3.927809668136462*^9, {
    3.927824738709173*^9, 3.927824755009655*^9}, {3.92822730717468*^9, 
    3.9282273204334497`*^9}, 3.928228218301458*^9, {3.92822931314583*^9, 
    3.928229313262317*^9}, 3.928246211407091*^9, 3.928252508706396*^9, 
    3.928325982696624*^9, 3.928326164009709*^9, 3.928400234639366*^9, 
    3.928407402508316*^9, 3.928489752817902*^9, 3.929436964790416*^9, 
    3.932823164669265*^9, 3.932823265326679*^9, 3.932823298317299*^9, 
    3.932823335089409*^9, 3.932833382061751*^9, {3.932833616599318*^9, 
    3.932833617429847*^9}},ExpressionUUID->
  "972fb5a0-9814-4a3c-8625-342bb3832866"],
 "\n\nThis corresponds to the picture on the left below.  Once the interior \
of the dotted circle has been resolved (i.e. given a choice of clasp or \
buckle for every edge) there will be 6 arcs ending at the boundary of the \
region with endpoints numbered 1 to 12 needed to match up with the arcs in \
the cap.  Thus, we must convert the precap into a picture like the one on the \
right, below.  Some intersections of arcs must be decorated by a buckle, \
because if one began with a plane graph, and chose clasps or buckles at each \
edge, arcs such as arc[4,8] and arc[5,9] below would have to interact in at \
least 1 buckle (the arcs might interact more than once, but on interaction is \
enough to record that these two arcs must be colored differently).\n\n",
