  "98020b9c-58e9-4219-b569-d4f45bbcbd46"],
 "\nThere are, of course, multiple possible caps for a given a PreCap.  Any \
crossings between two arcs that come together at a single spoke on the \
boundary of the hexagonal region may be ignored, since the calculations we \
will do already consider the insertion of a clasp or buckle at such edges (an \
extra clasp or buckle would be redundant in the same way that multiple edges \
do not change the chromatic polynomial).  For example, all three of the \
following caps should be considered equivalent.  \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
