Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Sifting out the nonplanar", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.932823940776684*^9, 3.932823952478187*^9}, {
  3.933082258835885*^9, 3.933082268344513*^9}, {3.933082622220318*^9, 
  3.93308262272716*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ad33d7ae-5cc0-4ba0-ab29-\
7502d3750778"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At this point SixCaps contains all planar six caps, but also contains some \
caps which are only possible in states of nonplanar graphs.  For example, \
notice in the figure below that arc[3,10] must separate arc[1,12] (and \
arc[2,11]) from arc[5,8].  Any cap that contains V[1,5], but contains neither \
a V[1,3] nor a V[3,5], cannot occur in a state for a planar graph.  The code \
below sifts out such caps (as well as rotationally symmetric versions), \
leaving only the SixCaps that can occur in a state for a planar graph.\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
